  ($q$cs-58$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Even as flood warnings poured in through the night, the broadcaster's voice remained ______, never wavering into panic despite the escalating danger.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["steady","frantic","hesitant","calm"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$'Never wavering' emphasizes consistency sustained over the whole night, which 'steady' names directly; 'calm' describes a lack of distress at a given moment but doesn't by itself imply the voice held constant despite escalating danger.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-59$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A science article begins by asserting that life cannot exist without sunlight, then describes the discovery of thriving ecosystems around deep-sea hydrothermal vents that rely on chemical energy instead, using the vents to overturn the assumption stated at the outset.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the description of the deep-sea vents in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It provides a counterexample that overturns the assumption presented in the opening sentence.","It confirms the assumption presented in the opening sentence.","It qualifies the opening claim as a rare exception rather than truly overturning it.","It summarizes the article's conclusion before any evidence is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The passage states directly that the vents are used 'to overturn the assumption stated at the outset,' not merely to carve out a minor exception to it, making the correct answer the accurate description of their function.$q$, null),
