  ($q$cs-76$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Throughout the tense trial, the lead juror kept an ______ expression, giving neither attorney any hint of her eventual vote.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["impassive","animated","sympathetic","stoic"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clue concerns what her face revealed — 'impassive' names an expression that gives nothing away — while 'stoic' describes an attitude of enduring hardship without complaint, which doesn't necessarily describe a blank, unreadable expression.$q$, null),
