  ($q$cs-114$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Participants in the study reported feeling ______ after only ten minutes of the guided breathing exercise, with measured heart rates dropping noticeably.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["calmer","anxious","energized","distracted"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Heart rates 'dropping noticeably' after a breathing exercise indicates participants felt calmer, not anxious or energized.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-115$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The guidebook described the mountain trail as ______, warning hikers that a single wrong turn in dense fog could leave them miles off course.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["treacherous","straightforward","scenic","crowded"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A warning that 'a single wrong turn...could leave [hikers] miles off course' describes a treacherous trail, not a straightforward one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-116$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The renovated train station was praised as ______, preserving the original nineteenth-century facade while housing entirely new, modern platforms inside.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["harmonious","incongruous","dilapidated","temporary"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Preserving the old facade while adding modern platforms inside describes a harmonious blend of old and new, not an incongruous one.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-117$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The novel's structure is ______, jumping between five different narrators' perspectives without warning from chapter to chapter.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["fragmented","linear","predictable","simple"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Jumping between five narrators 'without warning' describes a fragmented structure, the opposite of linear or simple.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-118$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Historians now consider the treaty's effects ______, since it simultaneously ended one conflict and planted the seeds for another decades later.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["paradoxical","straightforward","negligible","beneficial"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A treaty that both 'ended one conflict' and 'planted the seeds for another' has contradictory effects, which 'paradoxical' captures.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-119$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The survey results were ______, since responses from urban and rural participants differed by less than two percentage points on every question.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["uniform","polarized","inconclusive","biased"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Responses differing 'by less than two percentage points' across groups describes uniform results, not polarized ones.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-120$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The philosopher's argument was ______, resting on a single assumption that, if false, would cause the entire conclusion to collapse.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["precarious","airtight","fragile","circular"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$An argument that would 'collapse' if one assumption failed is precariously balanced on that single point; 'fragile' suggests general delicacy but doesn't capture the specific dependency on one assumption the way 'precarious' does.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-121$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The researchers' claim was ______, supported by only a single small-scale trial that other labs had not yet attempted to replicate.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["tentative","definitive","preliminary","widely confirmed"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The claim's weakness is its lack of replication, making it cautiously held, or tentative; 'preliminary' would describe its place early in a research timeline, but a finding can be preliminary and still stated with confidence, so it doesn't capture the hedging the unreplicated trial demands.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-122$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The critic argued that the author's prose, for all its surface beauty, was fundamentally ______, since the ornate sentences rarely advanced the plot or revealed character.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["superfluous","essential","concise","decorative"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The critic's complaint is that the ornate prose serves no narrative function — superfluous means wholly unnecessary to the work's substance — while 'decorative' would concede the prose serves an aesthetic purpose, which the critic denies by saying it never advances plot or character.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-123$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The contract's clause was deliberately ______, allowing either party to interpret the obligation differently should a dispute arise.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["ambiguous","explicit","vague","standard"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clause supports two distinct, competing readings by design, which 'ambiguous' captures precisely; 'vague' would mean merely imprecise or unclear, not necessarily allowing two parties to construct different coherent interpretations.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-124$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The senator's proposal was ______ in its scope, addressing tax policy, healthcare, education funding, and immigration within a single bill.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["omnibus","narrow","modest","comprehensive"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The clue is not just thoroughness but bundling unrelated subjects — tax, healthcare, education, immigration — into one bill, which 'omnibus' names specifically; 'comprehensive' could describe exhaustive coverage of a single topic without that multi-subject bundling.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-125$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The curator defended the exhibit's unconventional pairing of medieval tapestries with video art as ______, arguing the juxtaposition revealed unexpected continuities between eras.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["inspired","arbitrary","offensive","unconventional"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The curator isn't just noting the pairing was unusual — she's defending its insight, that it 'revealed unexpected continuities'; 'unconventional' would only describe its novelty, not the justified creative vision 'inspired' conveys.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-126$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$Analysts described the central bank's messaging as ______, since each official statement seemed to hint at a different timeline for interest rate changes.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["inconsistent","transparent","unanimous","nuanced"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Analysts' complaint is that the statements didn't line up with each other, suggesting no stable position — 'inconsistent' — rather than that each statement offered a carefully calibrated, more complex view, which 'nuanced' would suggest without implying contradiction.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-127$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on urban beekeeping opens by describing a rooftop hive producing jars of honey in its first season, then explains the specific flowering plants in the surrounding neighborhood that made the yield possible.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It explains a specific cause behind the result described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the claim made in the first sentence.","It introduces an unrelated hobby.","It states the article's conclusion before any evidence is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence explains the specific flowering plants that caused the strong honey yield described in the first sentence, functioning as a causal explanation.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-128$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A short piece on community gardens begins by noting that empty lots often attract litter and neglect, then describes how one neighborhood converted such a lot into a thriving vegetable garden tended by residents.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It presents a concrete solution to the problem raised in the first sentence.","It disputes that empty lots attract litter.","It shifts to a discussion of a different city issue.","It concludes the piece without offering any supporting detail."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence directly answers the problem of neglected lots raised in the first sentence by describing a thriving garden as a concrete response.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-129$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An article on a local bakery opens with a description of the aroma of fresh bread filling the street each morning, then broadens to profile the baker's decades-long apprenticeship, and closes with a note about her plans to open a second location.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It moves from a vivid sensory detail to background history to a glimpse of future plans.","It presents two competing bakeries and compares their products.","It opens with future plans and works backward to her childhood.","It argues that one bakery is superior to all others in the city."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The article's stated progression — aroma, then history, then future plans — matches the correct answer exactly.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-130$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A nature documentary script opens by showing a single monarch butterfly departing on its migration, then widens to explain the thousands of miles the species travels as a whole, and ends by noting the conservation threats facing the species.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It begins with a specific example, broadens to general information, and ends with a concern.","It presents two rival theories about butterfly migration.","It opens with a policy proposal and ends with an unrelated anecdote.","It compares monarch butterflies to a different insect species throughout."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text moves from one butterfly's departure (specific example) to the species' migration as a whole (general information) to conservation threats (a concern), matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-131$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$An essay on a small-town library begins by describing its crowded, outdated reading room, then explains that a recent grant allowed the library to double its space and add a children's section.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It presents a change that resolves the problem introduced in the first sentence.","It contradicts the description given in the first sentence.","It introduces an unrelated library in a different town.","It proves that the library never needed more space."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence describes a grant that doubled the library's space, directly resolving the crowding problem introduced in the first sentence.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-132$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$A profile of a long-distance swimmer opens with an account of her failing to finish her first open-water race, then explains that the setback led her to hire a coach who redesigned her training from the ground up.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It connects an early setback described in the first sentence to a change in her approach.","It contradicts the claim made in the first sentence.","It introduces a completely unrelated competition.","It states the profile's conclusion before any details are given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence explains how the failure described in the first sentence led her to hire a coach and change her training, linking the two sentences.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-133$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on the history of umbrellas opens by noting that early umbrellas were used almost exclusively by women as a fashion accessory, then argues that only after the 1850s did they become common, gender-neutral protection against rain, tracing the shift through period advertisements.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To trace a shift in how umbrellas were used and perceived over time","To argue that umbrellas should only be used as fashion accessories","To provide a technical manual for manufacturing umbrellas","To praise a single advertisement from the 1850s"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The essay opens with umbrellas' original use, then traces a shift toward common, gender-neutral use after the 1850s, matching the correct answer's description of the purpose.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-134$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A report on a local theater's renovation opens with a description of the leaking roof that forced its closure, presents in its middle section the fundraising campaign that paid for repairs, and closes with the sold-out reopening night.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the middle section of the report?$q$, $q$["To explain how the problem described in the opening was ultimately resolved","To contradict the claims made in the report's opening","To define technical terms related to theater architecture","To criticize the donors who funded the renovation"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The middle section's fundraising campaign explains how the roof problem from the opening was resolved, leading to the reopening described at the end.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-135$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on handwriting instruction opens by acknowledging that most schools have phased out cursive lessons, then spends its remaining paragraphs arguing that cursive still offers unique benefits for fine motor development that typing cannot replicate.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the rhetorical strategy used in the text?$q$, $q$["Acknowledging a trend before arguing against abandoning the practice entirely","Ignoring the decline of cursive instruction to focus solely on typing","Presenting only anecdotal evidence without any structured argument","Avoiding any clear position on whether cursive should be taught"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Acknowledging the decline of cursive instruction before arguing for its unique benefits is a concede-then-argue strategy, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-136$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An article on coral reefs opens with a diver's firsthand account of a vibrant, colorful reef, then presents data showing that nearby reefs without the same protections have lost most of their coral cover.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It supplies comparative evidence that highlights the value of the protections mentioned in the first sentence.","It contradicts the diver's firsthand account.","It introduces an unrelated marine species.","It concludes the article before any data has been presented."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence contrasts unprotected reefs with the protected one in the first sentence, supplying comparative evidence for the value of protection.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-137$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A biography of a chess-playing computer program spends its early chapters on the engineers' repeated failures to beat human champions, then devotes a full chapter to the single match in which the program finally succeeded, treating it as the culmination of the project.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the chapter devoted to that single match?$q$, $q$["It highlights a pivotal success that the biography treats as the project's turning point.","It disproves the claims made earlier about the engineers' failures.","It shifts entirely away from chess to focus on unrelated technology.","It summarizes the whole project before any details are given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text explicitly frames the single winning match as 'the culmination of the project,' so the chapter functions to highlight that pivotal success.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-138$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on lighthouse keepers opens by romanticizing the solitude of the job, then spends its final section describing the extreme isolation that drove many keepers to request transfers after only a single winter.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final section in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It complicates the earlier romanticized view by introducing a harsher reality of the job.","It repeats the praise offered in the opening without adding anything new.","It shifts the topic entirely away from lighthouse keepers.","It proves that no lighthouse keeper ever found the job difficult."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$After romanticizing the solitude of the job, the final section introduces the isolation that drove keepers to leave, complicating rather than repeating the earlier praise.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-139$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A museum essay on ancient pottery opens by describing the intricate geometric patterns visible on a surviving vase, then explains that similar patterns appear on textiles from the same region, suggesting a shared decorative tradition across crafts.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It extends the observation in the first sentence to suggest a broader cultural pattern.","It disputes the claim that the vase has geometric patterns.","It argues that pottery and textiles were never produced in the same region.","It shifts the essay's focus to an unrelated artifact with no connection to the vase."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence extends the pattern observed on the vase to textiles, suggesting a shared tradition across crafts rather than disputing or ignoring the first sentence.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-140$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An article on competitive debate opens by describing a single student's halting, nervous first speech, then traces her development over four years of practice rounds and tournaments, and closes with her delivering a confident closing argument at the national championship.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It follows a chronological arc from early struggle to eventual mastery.","It presents two debaters and compares their styles side by side.","It opens with the national championship and works backward to her first speech.","It argues that nervousness is required for success in debate."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text follows a clear chronological progression from a nervous first speech to eventual confident mastery, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-141$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on a controversial dam project acknowledges the economic benefits its supporters cite, then spends several paragraphs detailing the ecological costs to downstream communities, without ever directly stating whether the dam should have been built.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the rhetorical strategy used in the text?$q$, $q$["Presenting both benefits and costs while leaving the overall judgment to the reader","Praising the dam directly without mentioning any drawbacks","Ignoring all economic considerations in favor of personal opinion","Stating a firm conclusion before presenting any evidence"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Presenting both the economic benefits and ecological costs without stating a final judgment leaves the overall assessment to the reader, matching the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-142$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay opens by asserting that handwritten letters had become entirely obsolete by the early twenty-first century, then describes a resurgence of letter-writing clubs among young people who cite the format's slowness as its appeal, using this trend to challenge the essay's own opening claim.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the description of letter-writing clubs in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It provides a counterexample that undermines the assumption presented in the opening sentence.","It confirms the assumption presented in the opening sentence.","It qualifies the opening claim as true only for business correspondence, not personal letters.","It summarizes the essay's conclusion before any evidence is given."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The passage states the trend is used 'to challenge the essay's own opening claim' directly, not to carve out a narrower exception for it, so the letter-writing clubs function as a counterexample undermining that assumption.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-143$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$A history of a shipping canal devotes its opening section to the engineering challenges of its construction, its middle section to the political disputes between the nations that funded it, and its final section to the economic transformation it brought to global trade routes.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It examines a single subject through three distinct lenses: technical, political, and economic.","It presents a single case study and dismisses its importance entirely.","It begins with economic transformation and works backward to construction.","It argues that the canal's construction was not politically significant."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The three sections examine the canal through engineering, political, and economic lenses in turn, matching the correct answer's description of multiple perspectives on one subject.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-144$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay begins by praising a factory town's rapid economic growth in the early twentieth century, then spends its final paragraphs detailing the long-term health consequences residents faced from industrial pollution that the growth figures never captured.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the final paragraphs in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["They complicate the earlier praise by revealing a cost the growth figures obscured.","They repeat the praise offered in the opening paragraphs without adding anything new.","They shift the focus to a neighboring factory town that avoided industrial pollution.","They prove that the factory town experienced no economic growth at all."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$After praising economic growth, the final paragraphs reveal a health cost in the same town that the growth figures missed, complicating rather than repeating the earlier praise or shifting to a different town altogether.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-145$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on a philosopher's reputation opens by summarizing the harsh dismissal her work received from contemporaries, then spends the remainder of the piece tracing how later scholars, working decades after her death, came to regard her as a founder of an entirely new field.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To trace how a thinker's critical reputation shifted dramatically after her death","To argue that her contemporaries were correct to dismiss her work","To argue that her contemporaries' harsh dismissal permanently ended her influence","To defend the harsh dismissal she initially received"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The essay traces the philosopher's reputation from harsh contemporary dismissal to later recognition as a founder of a new field, not a permanently ended influence, matching the correct answer's description of a reputational shift.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-146$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Exercise scientist A argues that morning workouts burn more fat than evening workouts, citing a study showing higher fat oxidation rates in participants who exercised before breakfast.

Text 2: Exercise scientist B argues that workout timing makes no meaningful difference to fat loss over time, citing a longer study in which total body composition changes were nearly identical between morning and evening exercisers.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two scientists' views?$q$, $q$["Scientist A emphasizes short-term fat oxidation, while Scientist B emphasizes long-term body composition outcomes.","Both scientists agree that workout timing has no effect on fat loss.","Scientist B relies exclusively on short-term fat oxidation data.","Scientist A argues that evening workouts are more effective than morning workouts."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Scientist A's evidence concerns short-term fat oxidation, while Scientist B's longer study measured overall body composition change, the contrast described in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-147$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Animal trainer A argues that reward-based methods alone are sufficient to correct most dog behavior problems, citing faster progress in dogs trained only with treats and praise.

Text 2: Animal trainer B argues that reward-based methods work well for simple commands but are insufficient for serious aggression issues, which require a structured program combining rewards with clear boundaries.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two trainers' views?$q$, $q$["Trainer A sees reward-based methods as generally sufficient, while Trainer B sees them as insufficient for serious cases.","Both trainers agree that rewards should never be used in dog training.","Trainer B relies exclusively on treats and praise for aggression issues.","Trainer A argues that aggression issues require a different program entirely."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Trainer A sees reward-based methods as broadly sufficient, while Trainer B sees them as inadequate for serious aggression cases requiring added structure — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-148$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Coffee roaster A recommends grinding beans immediately before brewing, arguing that pre-ground coffee loses aromatic compounds within minutes of grinding.

Text 2: Coffee roaster B recommends buying pre-ground coffee for most home drinkers, arguing that the convenience outweighs a flavor difference most casual drinkers cannot detect.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the relationship between the two roasters' recommendations?$q$, $q$["Roaster B prioritizes convenience over the flavor concern that Roaster A considers most important.","Both roasters agree that pre-ground coffee should never be purchased.","Roaster A recommends pre-ground coffee for most home drinkers.","Roaster B argues that grinding immediately before brewing is essential."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Roaster B explicitly values convenience over the flavor loss Roaster A emphasizes, matching the trade-off described in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-149$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 1, $q$Text 1: Education researcher A argues that spacing study sessions across several days produces better long-term retention than cramming the same material into one long session.

Text 2: Education researcher B argues that for simple memorization tasks, a single intensive session can produce retention nearly as strong as spaced sessions, though the advantage of spacing grows with more complex material.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the relationship between the two researchers' findings?$q$, $q$["Researcher B's findings partly qualify Researcher A's claim, suggesting the advantage of spacing depends on task complexity.","Researcher B's findings directly contradict Researcher A's claim in every case.","Both researchers studied only complex memorization tasks.","Researcher A found that cramming always works better than spacing."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Researcher B's finding that cramming works nearly as well for simple tasks qualifies, rather than flatly contradicts, Researcher A's general claim about spacing.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-150$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Workplace researcher A argues that employees working from home report higher productivity, citing self-reported output surveys showing increased task completion.

Text 2: Workplace researcher B argues that self-reported surveys overstate productivity gains, citing time-tracking software data showing many remote employees take longer breaks than survey responses suggest.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the relationship between the two researchers' claims?$q$, $q$["Researcher B's data challenges the reliability of the method Researcher A relies on.","Researcher B's findings confirm exactly what Researcher A argues.","Both researchers used identical time-tracking methods.","Researcher A argues that self-reported surveys are unreliable."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Researcher B's time-tracking data questions the accuracy of the self-reported surveys Researcher A relies on, challenging that method's reliability.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-151$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Paleontologist A argues that a species of small dinosaur hunted in coordinated packs, citing trackway fossils showing multiple individuals moving together at matched speeds.

Text 2: Paleontologist B argues that the same trackways more likely reflect individuals migrating along the same route at different times, since the tracks show no evidence of the animals interacting with one another.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two paleontologists' interpretations?$q$, $q$["Paleontologist A interprets the trackways as evidence of coordinated group behavior, while Paleontologist B interprets them as unrelated individual movement.","Both paleontologists agree the trackways show no evidence of movement.","Paleontologist B argues the dinosaurs hunted in coordinated packs.","Paleontologist A relies exclusively on evidence of interaction between individuals."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Paleontologist A reads the trackways as coordinated group behavior, while Paleontologist B reads the same evidence as unrelated individual movement — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-152$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Energy analyst A argues that large-scale battery storage is the most practical way to stabilize a power grid that relies heavily on solar and wind.

Text 2: Energy analyst B argues that pumped hydro storage remains more practical at large scale than batteries, since it can store far more energy per dollar despite requiring specific geography.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two analysts' views?$q$, $q$["Analyst A favors battery storage, while Analyst B favors pumped hydro storage.","Both analysts agree that grid storage is unnecessary.","Analyst B argues that batteries are the cheaper option at large scale.","Analyst A argues that pumped hydro requires no specific geography."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Analyst A favors batteries, while Analyst B favors pumped hydro for its cost-per-energy advantage at scale — the contrast captured in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-153$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Archaeologist A argues that an ancient coastal population relied primarily on fish for protein, citing isotope analysis of bone collagen consistent with a marine diet.

Text 2: Archaeologist B argues that the same population relied mainly on hunted land animals, citing tool assemblages dominated by projectile points typically used for hunting large game.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes a key difference between the two archaeologists' views?$q$, $q$["Archaeologist A points to isotope evidence for a marine diet, while Archaeologist B points to tool evidence for a land-based diet.","Both archaeologists agree the population ate no fish or land animals.","Archaeologist B relies exclusively on isotope analysis.","Archaeologist A argues the population hunted large land animals."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Archaeologist A cites isotope evidence for a marine diet, while Archaeologist B cites tool evidence for a land-based diet — the contrast in the correct answer.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-154$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Marketing researcher A argues that humorous advertisements are more memorable than serious ones, citing recall tests in which viewers remembered humorous ads days later.

Text 2: Marketing researcher B argues that humorous ads are memorable but less persuasive, citing purchase-intent surveys showing serious ads more often convinced viewers to buy the product.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the relationship between the two researchers' findings?$q$, $q$["Researcher B's findings complicate Researcher A's by distinguishing memorability from persuasiveness.","Researcher B's findings exactly replicate Researcher A's results.","Both researchers found that serious ads are more memorable.","Researcher A found that humorous ads are less persuasive than serious ones."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Researcher B's distinction between memorability and persuasiveness adds nuance to, rather than simply repeats, Researcher A's claim about humorous ads.$q$, null),
  ($q$cs-155$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: City planner A argues that planting fast-growing tree species is the best way to quickly expand urban shade coverage, citing their rapid canopy development within a few years.

